1
00:00:00,741 --> 00:00:02,041
(Sheldon:)Obesity.

2
00:00:04,177 --> 00:00:06,247
(Bernadette:)I have the tool you wanted.

3
00:00:06,246 --> 00:00:07,676
(Leonard:)Thank you.

4
00:00:07,681 --> 00:00:09,581
(Raj:)You guys don't have
to go to the trouble.

5
00:00:09,583 --> 00:00:10,913
I'm back in the money now;

6
00:00:10,918 --> 00:00:12,318
(Raj:)I can just buy
another helicopter.

7
00:00:12,319 --> 00:00:13,389
(Howard:)It's not about the money.

8
00:00:13,387 --> 00:00:14,817
(Howard:)It's about solving a problem.

9
00:00:14,822 --> 00:00:16,222
(Howard:)It's why I became an engineer.

10
00:00:16,223 --> 00:00:18,693
(Howard:)It's what I like to do,
it's what I'm trained to do.

11
00:00:18,692 --> 00:00:20,762
(Howard:)It's who I am.

12
00:00:20,761 --> 00:00:23,491
(Sheldon:)Oh, look at you--
the little engineer that could.

13
00:00:25,331 --> 00:00:27,231
(Bernadette:)Why don't you just
call tech support?

14
00:00:27,234 --> 00:00:30,064
Hey!
Whoa!
Not cool!

15
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:31,270
(Penny:)What?

16
00:00:31,271 --> 00:00:32,771
(Howard:)There's two kinds of
people in this world:

17
00:00:32,773 --> 00:00:34,373
(Howard:)those who call
tech support

18
00:00:34,374 --> 00:00:37,744
(Howard:)and those who make fun of the
people who call tech support.

19
00:00:37,745 --> 00:00:39,275
(Bernadette:)I call tech support
all the time.

20
00:00:39,279 --> 00:00:40,609
Ha-ha!
You call tech support!

21
00:00:40,614 --> 00:00:42,314
What a baby!

22
00:00:43,449 --> 00:00:46,349
(Headmaster:)And now, for our
commencement address,

23
00:00:46,353 --> 00:00:48,853
(Headmaster:)one of our
most distinguished alumni,

24
00:00:48,856 --> 00:00:53,796
(Headmaster:)noted Caltech physicist
Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

25
00:00:57,597 --> 00:00:59,967
(Leonard(on screen):)Members of the faculty,
students,

26
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:02,697
(Leonard(on screen):)I'm excited to speak
to you today.

